From: AEON-7 <aeon-7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:59:05 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] [ROCm][Inkling2] Per-pass KV caches and conv states for
 looped layers

Looped layers (6..17, 3 passes) keep one attention KV cache and one
short-conv state per pass, following the upstream NVIDIA design in
vllm/models/inkling2/nvidia/{attention,loop}.py (PR #69028, Apache-2.0):
Inkling2AttentionPassCache registers .pass{p} attention layers, the conv
states get .conv_state.pass{p}, forward() takes pass_idx, and the short
conv accepts an owner override. The fused QKV projection is used only
when all three inputs alias. Ported to the AMD package by AEON-7.

Signed-off-by: AEON-7 <aeon-7@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 vllm/models/inkling2/amd/attention.py | 121 +++++++++++++++++++++-----
 vllm/models/inkling2/amd/sconv.py     |  15 +++-
 2 files changed, 111 insertions(+), 25 deletions(-)

